🚀 MASTER BUILD PROMPT (FULL SYSTEM SCAFFOLD)

You are to generate a complete production-ready multi-app system for an import-based retail business. The system must be built as a monorepo-style architecture with separate folders for each application, but sharing a consistent backend (Supabase/PostgreSQL).

1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW

Build a full commerce operating system consisting of:

Applications
admin-dashboard (Next.js)
pos-system (Next.js PWA with offline support)
mobile-app (React Native Expo)
shared-backend (Supabase schema + edge functions)
2. CORE BUSINESS DOMAIN

The system must support:

Product importation from multiple suppliers
Shipments with 1,000–2,000 items per batch
Inventory tracking using batches + serial numbers
Real-time POS sales (walk-in customers)
Customer management (retail + wholesale)
Credit sales system (customers can owe money)
Agent/referral commission wallet system
Withdrawal system (mobile money payouts via API)
Full accounting (profit, expenses, revenue)
Multi-role staff system
Audit logs for every sensitive action
Future support for multi-vendor marketplace
3. ARCHITECTURE REQUIREMENTS
Frontend
Next.js (Admin + POS)
React Native Expo (Mobile app)
Shared UI components where possible
Backend
Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Realtime)
Edge Functions for:
commission calculation
wallet updates
withdrawals
stock movements
credit updates
4. MONOREPO STRUCTURE

Generate project structure like:

/apps
  /admin-dashboard
  /pos-system
  /mobile-app

/packages
  /ui (shared components)
  /utils
  /types

/supabase
  /migrations
  /functions
  /seed
5. DATABASE (MUST IMPLEMENT FULL SCHEMA)

Implement Supabase SQL migrations for:

Core Tables
users
roles
customers
products
product_variants
shipments
shipment_items
inventory_batches
inventory_units (serial tracking)
inventory_ledger (source of truth)
orders
order_items
payments
wallets
wallet_transactions
withdrawals
credit_accounts
credit_payments
expenses
audit_logs
6. BUSINESS LOGIC RULES (CRITICAL)
Inventory
NEVER store stock as a single number
stock must be derived from inventory_ledger
Pricing
support multiple cost prices per product via batches
profit must be calculated per batch
Sales

When a sale happens:

Create order
Deduct stock via ledger entry
Record payment
Update wallet commissions (if applicable)
Log audit event
Credit Sales
allow partial payments
maintain customer debt ledger
Wallet System
agents have internal wallet balance
earnings are credited internally first
withdrawals are processed separately
Withdrawals
create withdrawal request
verify wallet balance
send payout via external API (MoMo/Hubtel/Flutterwave simulation layer)
update status (pending → completed)
7. OFFLINE SUPPORT (POS SYSTEM)

POS must:

work without internet temporarily
store transactions locally (IndexedDB)
sync when connection is restored
prevent duplicate sales during sync
8. ROLES & PERMISSIONS

Implement role-based access:

admin
manager
cashier
inventory officer
agent
customer

Each role must have permission-based restrictions.

9. REQUIRED FEATURES PER APP
Admin Dashboard
full business control
reports
inventory management
shipments
credit monitoring
financial analytics
POS System
barcode scanning
quick search
offline-first sales
receipt generation (digital first, printer-ready later)
Mobile App
inventory scanning
stock receiving
basic POS view (optional)
future delivery module support
10. EDGE FUNCTIONS (SUPABASE)

Implement server-side logic for:

calculate commissions
update wallets
process withdrawals
handle stock movements
enforce credit rules
generate audit logs
11. AUDIT SYSTEM (MANDATORY)

Every action must log:

user
action type
before/after data
timestamp
12. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
scalable to 10,000+ products
support 1,000–2,000 items per shipment
resilient to network failure
optimized for fast POS usage
secure financial logic (no client-side trust)
13. OUTPUT EXPECTED

Generate:

Full monorepo folder structure
Supabase SQL migration files
Basic Next.js app scaffolds (admin + POS)
React Native Expo scaffold
Shared types and utilities package
Example edge functions (wallet + sales + withdrawal)
Basic API/service layer abstraction
Clear separation between apps
Minimal working UI for each app (not design-heavy, functional only)
14. IMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS
Do NOT merge apps into one codebase UI
Do NOT skip database design
Do NOT hardcode business logic in frontend
Keep system modular and scalable
Prioritize correctness over UI polish
15. GOAL

Create a production-grade foundation for an import retail business system that can later evolve into a multi-vendor marketplace.